+# Bomb Farm — Bounded V2.7 Proof Adaptation
+
+Date: 2026-10-08. Execution Owner: Codex. Authority: ChatGPT PLAN38 + PLAN39. Two representative pages: home / guide.how-to-play. Game Adaptation is an adoption method, not runtime data. Nine existing authorities remain the only technical truths; this record cites Config, Inventory, Content, Facts (unused/unchanged), Media Manifest, media decisions, semantic theme values, search (disabled), freshness/version semantics rather than copying their contracts.
+
+## Adoption identity and player decision
+
+Independent fan-wiki proof at the already recorded bombfarmwiki.wiki domain. Not deployed. Mine overview → How-to-Play; no promised entity database, Market or build tool. Ordinary MDX gives a direct answer, an observation loop, completion/stop conditions and manual links. Page truth/dates/sources live only in Page Inventory; article content/FAQ in Content. New content publication/update date is 2026-10-08; factual source accessedAt remains 2026-09-04. No new verification date, live model or inferred version.
+
+## Visual decision
+
+Existing BF PROJECT_BRIEF §§Visual direction / Implementation palette records dark mine brown/charcoal, mineral gold and cyan from first-party visual reference. Reuse only compatible values in existing semantic tokens, and compact interface-oriented type/density values. No selector, token or theme engine added. This provenance is historical visual evidence, not proof that colors identify the game. Strict masked recognition remains pending; mine/three-team/task context must carry real identification evidence. No copied game imagery or UI.
+
+## Original diagram authorship
+
+On 2026-10-08 Codex authored public/media/proof/three-team-switching.svg specifically for this proof using newly written primitive rectangles, one divider line and text. It was not copied/traced from old energy-rotation.svg, official art, Steam screenshots, UI, logos, characters or competitor material. There are no images, external references or scripts. This is the actual creation record of a new project-authored work, not a third-party permission decision or Human approval.
+
+The factual source is separately the official Steam URL recorded on 2026-09-04 in old BF Inventory guide.energy-rotation: players can switch between three teams to keep the mine running. Diagram numbering is editorial; no state, timing, energy amount or mandatory order. Authored width/height/viewBox are 1200×675. Manifest rightsRef points here solely for the new diagram's authorship; sourceUrl is factual provenance, not a screenshot license. The source old SVG remains unchanged and is not imported. Official battle-overview.webp remains unauthorized and absent.
+
+## Media and journey decision
+
+One informative image, zero videos. Existing hero mappings serve home and How-to-Play. The article explains three choices rather than a recovery cycle; no gallery or empty media shell. Decision Table records actual integration and project authorship but leaves human_decision and visual_gate_state PENDING. No final approval is created.
+
+## Review and evidence
+
+Common Core/CI/tests/package/lock unchanged. BF exact ten input paths only. Real build/browser/masked results belong to the external proof package; do not store an acceptance state as reusable runtime data. WS04B/WS07/AX/Safari/RELEASE are not accepted by this adaptation. About still uses inherited Core editorial copy and must be disclosed as support-page residue; no Core fix in this proof.
